\end{figure}

Bootstrap 95\% CIs confirm non-overlapping $\sigma$ between pure and h3-1 but completely overlapping Jaccard across all hybrid ratios (\S\ref{ssec:statistical_methods}). Figure~\ref{fig:jaccard_hierarchy} shows a three-tier Jaccard hierarchy: independence baseline (${\sim}0.05$), cross-architecture (${\sim}0.10$, $2\times$ baseline), and within-architecture (${\sim}0.33$, $3\times$ cross-architecture; Appendix~\ref{app:within_arch_stability}). Pythia 70M seed calibration produces a comparable within-seed level ($J = 0.27$--$0.39$; Appendix~\ref{app:seed_calibration}), consistent with architecture-driven divergence, though matched multi-seed experiments would be needed for definitive evidence.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/fig_jaccard_hierarchy.pdf}
\caption{Jaccard hierarchy on LAMBADA (1.3B). Cross-architecture overlap ($\bar{J} \approx 0.09$) is $2\times$ the independence baseline but only one-third of within-architecture overlap ($\bar{J} \approx 0.33$). Pythia 70M within-seed Jaccard (different scale) falls at a comparable level. Error bars show the helped--hurt range.}
\label{fig:jaccard_hierarchy}
\end{figure}

Attention weight analysis (Appendix~\ref{app:attention_patterns}) shows GDN and RetNet produce nearly identical attention distributions (cosine 0.995) yet differ in per-example effects, suggesting these originate in the recurrent layers. The four-benchmark variation (Table~\ref{tab:multiplicity}) confirms independence: LAMBADA ($\alpha = 0.30$) is the only benchmark showing variance reduction despite having the highest multiplicity, while PIQA ($\alpha = 0.14$) and HellaSwag ($\alpha = 0.15$) show no variance reduction with the lowest multiplicity.

Cross-scale analysis confirms scale-robustness: pairwise Jaccard is stable ($\bar{J} = 0.08$--$0.10$ at both scales), though $\alpha$ is systematically higher at 340M ($\Delta \leq 8$\,pp). At 340M, aggregate variance reduction is absent ($\rho = -0.50$, $p = .45$), suggesting that the \emph{pattern} of multiplicity reflects structural differences while absolute magnitude is modulated by capacity (Appendix~\ref{app:scale_per_example}).
\subsection{Robustness}\label{ssec:robustness}

Removing GDN weakens the LAMBADA variance reduction pattern ($\rho = -0.7$, $p = .233$) and reverses MMLU's ($\rho = +0.6$), both driven by GDN's 16-head configuration (vs.\ 32 in others; Appendix~\ref{app:gdn_confound}). The RetNet--HGRN2 pair preserves the independence pattern ($\sigma \leq 0.008$, $J = 0.086$--$0.108$). The aggregate variance pattern is therefore dependent on GDN inclusion; the decoupling result is not. Five-architecture validation at 340M (GLA, DeltaNet added) confirms $J \leq 0.14$ across all ten pairs and four benchmarks (all $p < .01$; Figure~\ref{fig:jaccard_heatmap_5arch}; Appendix~\ref{app:extended_arch}). Full sensitivity analyses appear in Appendix~\ref{app:sensitivity}.

